# The build context is the repository root (docker-compose.yml's `build:`), so
# this file — not `app/.dockerignore`, which Docker never reads for a context
# that is not `app/` — is what keeps the context from being the whole checkout.
# On the server that checkout contains `pgdata/`, which is the live database.

.git
node_modules
app/node_modules
app/dist
app/test

# secrets, and the local crib sheet
.env
setupReference

# the data volume and the dumps, all bind-mounted next to this file on the
# server. `pgdata/` alone is gigabytes.
pgdata
backups
archive

*.log

# Only the built handbooks reach the image; `postbuild` copies them into
# dist/web to serve at /handbuch and /handbuch-lernende. The rest of docs/ is
# Markdown and a Puppeteer-driven generator with its own node_modules.
#
# **Both lines are needed, and this file is the one that bites.** `docs/*`
# excludes everything, so a new document is absent from the build *context* —
# which means the `COPY` in the Dockerfile fails with "can't stat" and reads
# like a missing file rather than an ignored one. 0.10.4 shipped with the
# Dockerfile and `postbuild` updated and this file not, and that is exactly how
# it failed.
docs/*
!docs/handbuch.html
!docs/handbuch-lernende.html

chalk-design-system
db
.github
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
